<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1,viewport-fit=cover"><meta name="theme-color" content="#101720"><title>ONE — The Last App | by Nathan Tabor</title><link rel="manifest" href="./manifest.webmanifest"><link rel="icon" href="../icon.svg">
<style>:root{font-family:system-ui,-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,sans-serif;color-scheme:dark;--bg:#0f141a;--card:#1b2630;--muted:#bfcbd2;--highlight:#e8dfc7;--line:#405361}*{box-sizing:border-box}body{margin:0;background:radial-gradient(circle at 25% -10%,#243d4a,transparent 38%),var(--bg);color:#f7f9fb}main{max-width:1120px;margin:auto;padding:15px 13px 96px}h1{font-size:clamp(2.8rem,8vw,5.5rem);line-height:.97;letter-spacing:-.075em;margin:10px 0 4px}h2{margin:0 0 8px;font-size:1.3rem}h3{font-size:1rem;margin:8px 0}p{color:var(--muted);line-height:1.55}small{font-size:.77rem;color:#aebdc6}button,input,select{font:inherit;border-radius:11px;background:#223543;color:#f4f6f8;border:1px solid #506575;padding:12px;max-width:100%}button{cursor:pointer}button:disabled{opacity:.5;cursor:not-allowed}button:focus-visible,input:focus-visible,select:focus-visible,a:focus-visible{outline:3px solid #e6d9b8;outline-offset:2px}input[type=text],input[type=date]{width:100%}label{font-size:.87rem;color:#c7d7e2;display:block;margin:8px 0 4px}a{color:#e1d4b4;text-decoration:none}.primary{background:#e9dfc6;color:#14212a;font-weight:800;border-color:#f0e4c9}.secondary{background:#283c49}.row{display:flex;gap:9px;flex-wrap:wrap;align-items:center}.between{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center;gap:9px;flex-wrap:wrap}.panel{border:1px solid #3e5361;border-radius:17px;background:#1b2630;padding:15px;margin:12px 0}.hero{border:1px solid #68736c;background:linear-gradient(145deg,#273f46,#16232d 65%,#1e2830);border-radius:21px;padding:clamp(19px,4vw,36px)}.hero p{max-width:680px}.eyebrow{font-size:.76rem;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.14em;font-weight:700;color:#dccba8}.stats{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(4,1fr);gap:8px}.stat{border:1px solid #4e626d;border-radius:12px;padding:10px;background:#263845}.stat strong{display:block;font-size:1.55rem}.nav{position:sticky;top:0;z-index:3;display:flex;gap:7px;padding:10px 0;overflow-x:auto;background:#0f141ae8;backdrop-filter:blur(12px)}.nav button{white-space:nowrap;padding:9px 11px}.nav [aria-current=page]{background:#e8dfc7;color:#15232e;font-weight:800}.domains{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(180px,1fr));gap:9px}.domain{text-align:left;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:5px;min-height:110px;background:#263643;border:1px solid #465b68;min-width:0}.domain strong{font-size:1.5rem;line-height:1;color:#e9d7aa}.domain span{font-weight:700}.domain small{line-height:1.35}.domain.selected{border-color:#f1d69e;background:#314954}.connectors{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(255px,1fr));gap:10px}.connector{border:1px solid #495f6d;border-radius:13px;padding:13px;background:#263846}.connector p{margin:7px 0;font-size:.9rem}.connector select{max-width:100%;font-size:.81rem}.flow{min-width:120px;text-transform:capitalize}.status{border-left:4px solid #d8c49b;background:#292f31;border-radius:5px;color:#ecf5f6;padding:12px;font-weight:600;margin:14px 0}.item{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:10px;padding:12px;border-bottom:1px solid #ffffff1d;overflow-wrap:anywhere}.item span{flex:1}.item input{width:20px;height:20px}.log{padding:9px 0;border-bottom:1px solid #ffffff18}.log p{margin:4px 0}.privacy{border-left:3px solid #d8bb86;padding:12px;background:#373125}.enabled{background:#a86260;border-color:#eb9b91}.blurb{font-size:.85rem;color:#b9c5cd}footer{font-size:.75rem;color:#b5c5ce;margin:30px 0}@media(max-width:600px){.stats{grid-template-columns:repeat(2,1fr)}.domains{grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr))}.domain{min-height:125px;padding:9px}.connectors{grid-template-columns:1fr}.hero{padding:17px}main{padding:10px 10px 84px}}[hidden]{display:none!important}</style></head><body><main>
<header class="between"><a href="../index.html">← TABOR FACTORY</a><span class="eyebrow">Personal Operating System · Preview</span></header>
<section class="hero"><div class="eyebrow">by Nathan Tabor</div><h1>ONE<span style="color:#ecdab3">.</span></h1><h2>The Last App</h2><p>Your world, your choice. Connect existing services where supported—or use ONE’s built-in tools. Separate modules, one control panel, explicit permissions.</p><div class="row"><span>✦ User-sovereign</span><span>✦ Modular</span><span>✦ Local-first</span></div></section>
<div class="nav" aria-label="ONE screens"><button data-view="home" aria-current="page">HOME</button><button data-view="items">MY ITEMS</button><button data-view="flows">FLOWS</button><button data-view="apps">APPS</button><button data-view="you">YOU</button><button data-view="architecture">101–901</button></div>
<section class="panel"><h2>DO · Quick command</h2><form id="one-do-form" class="row"><input id="one-do" type="text" aria-label="DO command" placeholder="Try: add task buy groceries" style="flex:1;min-width:210px" required><button class="primary" type="submit">DO <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></button></form><p class="blurb">Try “note project idea”, “open TABOR 1-2-3 FACTORY”, “run morning”, “show calendar”, or “zero mode”. Requests involving money, messages or bookings are blocked until real authorized services exist.</p><p id="one-status" class="status" role="status" aria-live="polite">ONE is ready. No third-party accounts are connected.</p></section>
<div data-page="home"><div id="one-stats" class="stats"></div><section class="panel"><div class="between"><h2>Life A–Z</h2><button id="one-zero" aria-pressed="false" class="secondary">Zero Mode: OFF</button></div><p>Choose the areas you want to use. These tiles become native functions or consent-based connections as ONE develops.</p><div id="one-domains" class="domains"></div></section></div>
<section data-page="items" hidden><div class="panel"><h2>Your built-in ONE</h2><p>Tasks, notes and events are currently local to this browser. They do not sync with Apple Reminders, Apple Notes or your calendars.</p><div id="one-items"></div></div><div class="panel"><h3>Add task</h3><form id="one-task-form" class="row"><input id="one-task" type="text" required maxlength="500" placeholder="What needs doing?" style="flex:1"><button type="submit" class="primary">Add</button></form><h3>Save note</h3><form id="one-note-form" class="row"><input id="one-note" type="text" maxlength="500" required placeholder="Your note" style="flex:1"><button type="submit">Save</button></form><h3>Schedule a local event</h3><form id="one-event-form" class="row"><input id="one-event" type="text" required maxlength="500" placeholder="Event name" style="flex:1"><input id="one-date" type="date" required><button type="submit">Add</button></form></div></section>
<section data-page="flows" hidden><div class="panel"><h2>FLOWS · Routines</h2><p>These demo flows change ONE’s local view and preferences; they do not turn on alarms, operate appliances or change system-wide focus modes.</p><div class="row" id="one-flows"></div><h3>How it will grow</h3><p>A production flow will show exactly which services are needed, which scopes are granted, any anticipated costs, the next actions and their approval checkpoints. High-risk actions cannot execute invisibly.</p></div></section>
<section data-page="apps" hidden><div class="panel"><h2>APPS · Connections Manager</h2><p>Official integrations only. Every provider starts disconnected. Choose read-only or approved action access only when that adapter is actually ready. A permission label is not authorization.</p><div id="one-providers" class="connectors"></div></div></section>
<section data-page="you" hidden><div class="panel"><h2>YOU · Your sovereignty</h2><p>ONE does not silently scan installed apps or control your phone’s operating system. Local data stays in this browser unless you export it. Clearing browser storage can erase it.</p><label><input id="one-quiet" type="checkbox"> Prefer quiet mode inside ONE</label><p>This does not change iPhone/Android notification permissions or Do Not Disturb.</p><div class="row"><button id="one-export">Export ONE data</button><button id="one-delete">Delete ONE local data</button><button id="one-help">Privacy details</button></div><div id="one-help-panel" class="privacy" hidden><p><strong>Device security:</strong> native apps need platform-specific permissions for calendar, health, contacts, files, app shortcuts and smart-home control. This website does not have them. OAuth tokens belong on an encrypted backend or in narrowly scoped native secure stores; the Secure Enclave is not a general OAuth token database. Payments require regulated provider integrations, transaction confirmation and compliance.</p></div></div><div class="panel"><h2>Action history</h2><div id="one-log"></div></div></section>
<section data-page="architecture" hidden><div class="panel"><h2>101–901 · The nine foundations</h2><p>This 101–901 module numbering belongs to ONE’s architecture, separate from the Factory’s 101–901 historical/creative portfolio categories. Both connect to TABOR ROOT, but neither overwrites the other.</p><div class="connectors">
<div class="connector"><strong>101 · Zero-UI</strong><p>Predictive frontend, privacy choices and DO control.</p></div><div class="connector"><strong>201 · Orchestration</strong><p>Consent-based provider adapters and allowed actions.</p></div><div class="connector"><strong>301 · Vault</strong><p>Portable private records and assets.</p></div><div class="connector"><strong>401 · Workflows</strong><p>Approvals, triggers and queues.</p></div><div class="connector"><strong>501 · Cloud</strong><p>Secure backend, latency and resilience.</p></div><div class="connector"><strong>601 · Identity</strong><p>Passkeys, protected grants and revocation.</p></div><div class="connector"><strong>701 · Payments</strong><p>Regulated finance APIs and explicit authorization.</p></div><div class="connector"><strong>801 · AI Routing</strong><p>Local semantic planning and confirmation gates.</p></div><div class="connector"><strong>901 · Native Bridge</strong><p>Permitted OS device capabilities.</p></div></div></div></section>
<footer>ONE — The Last App · by Nathan Tabor · Separate flagship project connected to TABOR 1-2-3 FACTORY. Local browser preview, not a replacement home screen or a finished universal phone controller.</footer>
</main><script src="./one.js" defer></script></body></html>